learnings:
  - 'World ID v4 exact API: signRequest({signingKeyHex, action, ttl}) from @worldcoin/idkit-core/signing (re-exports @worldcoin/idkit-server) returns {sig,nonce,createdAt,expiresAt}; map to RpContext {rp_id,nonce,created_at,expires_at,signature}. Selfie Check credential id is ''selfie''; React preset is selfieCheckLegacy({signal}) from @worldcoin/idkit; verify is POST developer.world.org/api/v4/verify/{rp_id} with the proof forwarded verbatim (no API key).'
  - 'Needs THREE creds, not two: WORLD_APP_ID + WORLD_RP_ID (public) and WORLD_RP_SIGNING_KEY (SECRET, server-only). action binds a proof to a session (agentic-purchase:<sessionId>) and must match between backend signRequest and the widget''s action prop.'
  - 'Security: the mock GET /verify page is disabled (409) in world mode so it can''t settle without a real proof. Cross-session proof replay is a remaining hardening TODO (verify the proof''s action/nullifier matches the target session).'
  - '@worldcoin/idkit bundles an ~870kB WASM (proof handling) — Vite bundles it fine as an asset. signRequest itself is pure JS (no WASM).'
  - 'Open items to confirm at world-mode test time: IDKit `environment` (staging vs production, tied to the World app) is currently omitted (defaults); may need setting. World verify response is currently treated as ok/not-ok on HTTP status only.'
